-- Evidence: `tab-keys.test.mjs`
+### §stable-tab-keys — closing a tab renumbers the others so keys stay contiguous
+- Since: 2026-10-23 (the maintainer overrode the 2026-09-02 decision, which kept keys stable and left gaps)
+- Decision: `closeTab` renumbers the remaining tabs in order to `t1..tn` and resets `next` to `n + 1`, so keys are
+  always contiguous, including after a later `openTab`.
+- Forbidden: leaving gaps in the key sequence after a close (`t1,t3`).
+- Rejected: stable keys that are never reused (the 2026-09-02 decision). The user overrode it on 2026-10-23.
+- Reason: the user explicitly overrode the earlier decision and wants contiguous keys. Known cost, from the
+  2026-08-29 incident: the key is also the React key and the URL state. If the key stays the React key, closing a tab
+  remounts every tab to its right and loses their scroll position and unsaved form input. Bookmarked `?tabs=` URLs
+  can also point at different tabs after a close.
+- Evidence: `tab-keys.test.mjs` ("close renumbers keys", "open after close continues without a gap")
